* German Ultra preamp: V1a shared by two channels (the optocouplers OC1 and OC2 choose), the overdrive channel (V1b, V2b, V3a,
* V3b cathode follower, tone stack with GAIN, TREBLE, BASS, MIDDLE and VOLUME), the clean channel (V4b, tone stack with GAIN,
* BASS, MIDDLE, TREBLE, PRESENCE and VOLUME), the relay that picks one of the two, V5a and V5b (effects loop in bypass) and the
* master. Transcribed from a schematic of the 120 W two-channel head ("for educational purposes: may contain value errors").
* C4 (no value on the drawing) is taken as 22n; the effects loop, the Line Out and the footswitch relays are not modelled.
*
* Units: k M, m u n p. Node "0" is ground. See engine/include/sas/netlist.h for the format.

* Rail (node X): driven from the power amp at run time; 470 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 470
* The guitar (or the pedal in front of the amp) behind a variable source resistance.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Supply decoupling: R33, R34 and R32 (10k, 10k, 6.8k) with K22, K21 (30 uF) and K20 (20 uF).
R R33 x nA 10k
C K22 nA 0 30u
R R34 nA nB 10k
C K21 nB 0 30u
R R32 nB nC 6.8k
C K20 nC 0 20u

* Input and V1a (shared by both channels).
R R1 in 0 100k
R R2 in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R5 nC p1 180k
C CX1 g1 p1 4.7p
R R6 k1 0 1.8k
C C3 k1 0 4.7u
C CX2 p1 pc 100n

* Channel switching (the optocouplers OC2 = overdrive and OC1 = clean). Position 0 of the channel selector is overdrive.
R SW_OC2 pc od1 1
R SW_OC1 pc cl1 1e12

* Overdrive channel: K5 and K4, GAIN (P1, 475k) with its bright capacitors, KX2 into V1b.
C K5 od1 od2 2.2n
C K4 od2 0 330p
R VR1T od2 w1 1
R VR1B w1 0 1
C C201 od2 w1 3n
C C202 od2 w1 300p
C KX2 w1 od3 22n
R R9 od3 0 68k
R R8 od3 g2 68k
T V1B g2 p2 k2 12AX7
R R7 nC p2 100k
R R10 k2 0 2.4k
C K3 k2 0 470n
C KX1 p2 d1 22n
R R12 d1 0 470k
R R13 d1 g3 330k
R R14 g3 0 330k
T V2B g3 p3 k3 12AX7
R R15 nC p3 100k
R R16 k3 y3 1.5k
C K12 y3 0 2.2u
R R17 y3 0 1.5k
C K8 p3 d2 22n
R R18 d2 0 470k
R R19 d2 g4 470k
T V3A g4 p4 k4 12AX7
R RX2 nB p4 100k
R RX1 k4 0 1k
T V3B p4 nB k5 12AX7
R R21 k5 0 100k

* Overdrive tone stack: R60 33k and C206 with TREBLE (P4, 470k with R70 across the lower part), C203 into BASS (P2, 1M) and
* MIDDLE (P3, 25k), C204 from the bass wiper, VOLUME (P6, 10k).
R R60 k5 jj 33k
C C206 k5 tp 330p
R VR4T tp wp 1
R VR4B wp jj 1
R R70 wp jj 270k
C C203 jj o1 47n
R VR2T o1 w2 1
R VR2B w2 m1 1
R VR3T m1 ov 1
R VR3B ov 0 1
C C204 w2 ov 22n
R VR6T ov odo 1
R VR6B odo 0 1

* Clean channel: the input network (R303, C305, C306 and RX5 into the node Q), BASS (P8, 220k) and R302, C303, R301 and
* C301 into GAIN (P7, 390k) and V4b, then its tone stack (CX5, R305, C309, TREBLE P10, C308, R306, C4, MIDDLE P9), the
* PRESENCE network (C310, P11, R320), R308 / C311 and the clean VOLUME (P12, 430k).
R R303 cl1 q 499k
C C305 cl1 q 680p
C C306 cl1 c6 3.3n
R RX5 c6 q 499k
R R302 q cq 340k
C C303 cl1 cq 150p
R VR8 q 0 1
R R301 cq t7 100k
C C301 cq t7 470p
R VR7T t7 w7 1
R VR7B w7 0 1
C C302 t7 w7 82p
T V4B w7 p5 k6 12AX7
R RX6 nA p5 100k
R R26A k6 0 1k
C K16 k6 0 10u
C CX5 p5 e0 47n
R R305 e0 e1 100k
C C309 e0 etp 330p
R VR10T etp ew 1
R VR10B ew e2 1
C C308 e1 e2 100n
R R306 e2 0 220k
C C4 e1 e3 22n
R VR9 e3 0 1
C C310 ew pr1 2.2n
R VR11 pr1 pr2 1
R R320 pr2 0 22k
R R308 ew cl2 360k
C C311 ew cl2 100p
R VR12T cl2 cw 1
R VR12B cw 0 1

* The relay RE101B: overdrive (normally closed) or clean, then V5a (R104 and R100 in its cathode, R103 returning the grid).
R SW_RB_NC odo vx 1
R SW_RB_NO cw vx 1e12
R R102 vx 0 1M
C C101 vx g6 100n
T V5A g6 p6 k7 12AX7
R R103 g6 cb 1M
R R104 k7 cb 470
R R100 cb 0 22k
R RX3 nA p6 22k

* Effects loop in bypass, V5b and the master (P13, 220k, a rheostat to ground) behind RX4.
C C100 p6 f1 1u
R R108 f1 v5g 180k
C C133 f1 v5g 22p
R R109 v5g 0 56k
T V5B v5g p7 k8 12AX7
R R106 nA p7 100k
R R110 k8 0 1.8k
C C102 p7 d3 100n
R RX4 d3 y 180k
R VR13 y 0 1
